<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Little Turtle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1747–1812</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Mihšihkinaahkwa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Little Turtle, Mihšihkinaahkwa in Miami, was a war leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miami-people">Miami people</a>. With the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shawnee">Shawnee</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blue-jacket">Blue Jacket</a> he led the Western Confederacy to victories over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josiah-harmar">Josiah Harmar</a> in 1790 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthur-st-clair">Arthur St. Clair</a> in 1791, the worst defeat of the US Army by Native Americans. After the confederacy's defeat at Fallen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">Timbers</a> he signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-greenville">Treaty of Greenville</a> in 1795 and afterwards worked for peace with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/little-turtle.jpg" alt="Little Turtle" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Little_Turtle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
